# {{project_name}}

An upgradeable smart contract with an admin-gated upgrade entrypoint,
generated by [soroban-forge](https://github.com/soroban-forge-labs/soroban-forge)
from the `upgradeable` template.

## Features

- **Admin-only upgrades**: Only the address set as `admin` at deploy time may
  call `upgrade()`, which invokes
  [`update_current_contract_wasm`](https://docs.rs/soroban-sdk/latest/soroban_sdk/deployer/struct.Deployer.html#method.update_current_contract_wasm)
  to replace the contract code.
- **Constructor-set admin**: The admin address is baked into instance storage
  and cannot be changed (a simple pattern — teams often extend this to a
  multi-sig or timelock).

## Develop

```sh
cargo test
stellar contract build
```

## Deploy to testnet

The constructor takes `admin`:

```sh
stellar contract deploy \
  --wasm target/wasm32v1-none/release/{{crate_name}}.wasm \
  --source-account <your-identity> \
  --network testnet \
  -- --admin <ADMIN_ADDRESS>
```

## Upgrade flow

1. Build the new contract wasm.
2. Compute its hash:
   ```sh
   stellar contract hash --wasm path/to/new_contract.wasm
   ```
3. Have the admin invoke `upgrade` with that hash:
   ```sh
   stellar contract invoke \
     --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
     --source-account <ADMIN_IDENTITY> \
     --network testnet \
     -- \
     upgrade \
     --new_wasm_hash <HEX_HASH>
   ```

### Risks

- **Irreversible without backup**: Once upgraded, the old code is gone from the
  contract's storage. Always deploy a test contract first and verify the new
  wasm thoroughly before upgrading production.
- **Admin key security**: Whoever controls the admin address controls the
  contract. Consider using a multi-sig or timelock as the admin rather than a
  single key.
- **Storage compatibility**: The new contract must correctly read any existing
  storage written by the old contract, or data loss may occur.

